<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Temple of Athena Alea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena">Athena</a> Alea at Tegea in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadia">Arcadia</a> was the centre of a regional cult of Athena by the 8th century BCE. After a fire in 395 BCE it was rebuilt in the 4th century BCE to designs by the sculptor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scopas">Scopas</a>, and was considered one of the finest temples of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/temple-of-athena-alea.jpg" alt="Temple of Athena Alea" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vereert at Dutch Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tegea.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
